\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Librarian Lauren Wubbels announced two special events: a discussion with best-selling author Adam Gidwitz about his newest book, \ldblquote Max in the Land of Lies\rdblquote , on March 5, 2025, from 4:30 PM - 5:30 PM, and a Magic Show for adults featuring Allen Oshiro on March 11, 2025, from 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM.\line\line Cultural Arts Coordinator Andrew Booras invited the community to the Juneteenth Listening Session at the Manhattan Beach Library Community Room on March 8, 2025, from 10:00 AM-11:00 AM.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson invited the community to attend the upcoming Town Hall at the Joslyn Community Center on April 2, 2025, from 6:00 PM-8:00 PM, as well as the Strategic Plan Community Workshop at the Police/Fire Community Room on March 5, 2025, from 6:00 PM-7:00 PM.\line\line Financial Services Manager Libby Bretthauer invited the community to participate in the City's online budget survey, available on the City website through March 31, 2025. The results will be shared at a future City Council meeting.\line\line Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell reminded residents that batteries cannot be disposed of in landfills. Battery collection bins are available at all Manhattan Beach Unified School District schools, as well as at City Hall and the Joslyn Community Center. Improper disposal of lithium batteries has been causing fires.\line\line\pard Mayor Howorth issued a Public Alert regarding sea lions and other marine mammals on local beaches due to domoic acid toxicosis in Los Angeles County. Residents are urged not to approach these animals, as it is both dangerous for them and for people. Disturbing them can cause additional stress.\cf1\i0\f1\par
